        "id": 1858130
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-04T21:49:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Should this API should match what we planned for registered devices (List\u003cDiscoveredDevice\u003e) instead of the event state. Are we tracking all of the discovered states as a list in the service so the full list would be helpful here?\n\nI\u0027m also thinking since DiscoveredDevice is immutable, it will be best to pass the full list in case we are trying to update e.g the name or isRegistered.\n\nAlso if we do this, we can probably drop the State enum b/c presence in the list or not determines the same.",
      "revId": "8a14462749816cb966ed9c2402fd49f775451461",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8f0a2e0f_54c274ae",
        "filename": "remoteauth/framework/java/android/remoteauth/DeviceDiscoveryCallback.java",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 55,
      "author": {
        "id": 2015173
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-08T04:53:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What you are referring will take place in RemoteAuthListener API.\n\nDiscovery is different, the devices are not necessarily in the DB yet, and I prefer not to keep a state for discovery, but just to be a proxy\n\nAs agreed offline marking as\n\nDone",
      "parentUuid": "2af745a8_7da98424",
      "revId": "8a14462749816cb966ed9c2402fd49f775451461",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a7e9eb75_1cdb6cbf",
        "filename": "remoteauth/framework/java/android/remoteauth/DeviceDiscoveryCallback.java",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 57,
      "author": {
        "id": 1858130
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-04T21:49:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When we reach timeout do we discard the discovered state in the service or is there anything the receiver needs to know about what the timeout means? E.g. could they take the discovered device object they received 3 hours ago and try to use it?",
      "revId": "8a14462749816cb966ed9c2402fd49f775451461",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "195f2fca_39954896",
        "filename": "remoteauth/framework/java/android/remoteauth/DeviceDiscoveryCallback.java",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 57,
      "author": {
        "id": 2015173
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-08T04:53:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I prefer not to keep a state of the discovery in RAS at all.\n\nThe way I thought about it, whenever registration request is received by the RAS, it will need to be verified for correctness regardless of if it was discovered 1 hr ago or 1 min ago, because I don\u0027t see that the time gives us any assurance about a success of the registration\nIt may fail due to different reasons, for example the device is not nearby anymore, or attestation fails, etc\nAll this will be verified during registration\nthe notification about timeout is just to allow the user to build a flow around it, not for RAM/RAS",
      "parentUuid": "a7e9eb75_1cdb6cbf",
      "revId": "8a14462749816cb966ed9c2402fd49f775451461",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
